// Arbitrary-precision real arithmetic for the special functions, on core
// `BigInt`: a fixed-point value, `mantissa / 2^bits`, with `bits` chosen from
// the decimal digits the caller wants.
//
// Fixed point rather than a binary float because the rounding is then a single
// shift the caller can state and test, which is what the fifty- and hundred-digit
// checks need. `moonnum`'s `Number` keeps its `Float` at `Double`, so its
// arbitrary precision is integers and fractions only; this package supplies the
// real number the transcendental functions need.
import {
  "moonbitlang/core/bigint",
  "moonbitlang/core/math",
}
